38
00:00:59,165 --> 00:01:00,726
and ask five questions.

39
00:01:00,726 --> 00:01:02,109
What do we want to achieve?

40
00:01:02,109 --> 00:01:03,651
Why this method in particular?

41
00:01:03,651 --> 00:01:05,632
Where is it applied, and where not?

42
00:01:05,632 --> 00:01:06,791
How do we measure it?

43
00:01:06,791 --> 00:01:08,782
And when did we last improve it?

44
00:01:08,782 --> 00:01:10,352
Any question with no answer…

45
00:01:10,352 --> 00:01:12,053
that’s exactly where to improve.

46
00:01:12,053 --> 00:01:14,436
In the EFQM Model,

47
00:01:14,436 --> 00:01:15,973
RADAR is the scale every

48
00:01:15,973 --> 00:01:17,202
criterion is assessed against.

49
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:19,679
The approach must be sound and integrated,

50
00:01:19,679 --> 00:01:21,109
deployment structured,

51
00:01:21,109 --> 00:01:23,548
and refinement built on measurement and learning.

52
00:01:23,548 --> 00:01:25,483
“Exists” means you have a paper…

53
00:01:25,483 --> 00:01:26,900
“Excellent” means you have a

54
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,034
loop that keeps turning.

55
00:01:28,034 --> 00:01:29,789
What if on a project

56
00:01:29,789 --> 00:01:31,193
everyone says “I’m responsible”…

57
00:01:31,193 --> 00:01:33,193
